      },
      "text": "```\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n|   THERMOPLASTICS    |     THERMOSETS      |     ELASTOMERS      |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| Linear / branched   | Cross-linked 3D     | Lightly cross-      |\n| chains — no bonds   | network — permanent | linked or strongly  |\n| between chains      | covalent bonds      | entangled chains    |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| Melt on heating     | Cannot melt —       | Large reversible    |\n| Resolidify on cool  | char/decompose      | deformation (~500%) |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| Recyclable by melt  | NOT recyclable by   | Partially recyclable|\n| process (in theory) | melt process        | (ground rubber)     |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| ~80% of global      | ~15% of global      | ~5% + rubber sector |\n| plastic production  | plastic production  | (tires, seals)      |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n| PE, PP, PVC, PET,   | Epoxy, polyester,   | NR, SBR, EPDM,     |\n| PS, ABS, Nylon, PC  | phenolic, PU rigid  | NBR, silicone, CR   |\n+---------------------+---------------------+---------------------+\n```"
    },
